WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.654 --> 00:00:04.676
- [Narrator] This is Jackson,
a 16-year-old golden eagle.

00:00:04.676 --> 00:00:07.259
(gentle music)

00:00:08.295 --> 00:00:10.773
We almost lost these beautiful birds,

00:00:10.773 --> 00:00:13.273
but now they're bouncing back.

00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:19.638
Golden eagles are excellent
hunters and extremely fast.

00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:23.623
Diving at speeds greater
than 150 miles per hour,

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.986
this makes the golden eagle

00:00:24.986 --> 00:00:28.105
one of the fastest animals on earth.

00:00:28.105 --> 00:00:30.353
When hunting, they use their sharp talons

00:00:30.353 --> 00:00:32.367
to grab their prey.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.545
Golden eagles have been
known to hunt animals

00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:37.715
as large as deer and gray wolves.

00:00:37.715 --> 00:00:39.421
Their feathers are dark brown

00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:43.501
with lighter golds around
their head and neck.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.345
In the 1960s, ranchers
feared that they were eating

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:50.551
their livestock and over 20,000 were shot.

00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:52.453
Since then, through education,

00:00:52.453 --> 00:00:54.328
their numbers have re-stabilized

00:00:54.328 --> 00:00:58.078
and their biggest threat
now is habitat loss.

00:00:59.373 --> 00:01:01.456
This is the golden eagle.

00:01:05.771 --> 00:01:08.354
(zooming ding)

